class.description:
[TextureStreamingSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"texture_streaming"[/code]: it stores whether textures are streamed and how much VRAM they may use, for the player. The settings resource is a [TextureStreamingSettings]; the file is [code]user://settings/texture_streaming.ini[/code] by default, in the format of [member ProjectSettings.settings/general/default_format] (or of its domain group [code]settings/<domain>/[/code]). If it does not exist yet, the file of the former domain name ([code]user://settings/video_texture_streaming.ini[/code]) is read once at startup and written under the new name; the old file is kept.
[b]When values take effect:[/b] [code]enabled[/code] needs a restart ([constant SettingsServer.SETTING_FLAG_RESTART_REQUIRED], see [method SettingsServer.get_restart_required_names]): the domain is applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_PRE_DISPLAY] and writes [member ProjectSettings.rendering/textures/streaming/enabled] before the renderers compile their shaders. [code]memory_budget_enabled[/code] takes effect on the next frame. [code]memory_budget_mb[/code], [code]min_lod[/code] and [code]max_lod[/code] go to [member TextureStreaming.memory_budget_mb_override], [member TextureStreaming.min_lod_override] and [member TextureStreaming.max_lod_override] at once; at startup they wait until the [TextureStreaming] singleton exists. The project settings are changed for the running game only; they are never saved to [code]project.godot[/code], and the domain does not change them in the editor.
The defaults are the project settings [code]rendering/textures/streaming/enabled[/code], [code]memory_budget_enabled[/code], [code]memory_budget_mb[/code], [code]min_lod[/code] and [code]max_lod[/code].
[b]Renderers and platforms:[/b] texture streaming works with the Forward+ and Mobile renderers (Windows, Linux, macOS, Android, iOS). The Compatibility renderer has no texture streaming: [method SettingsServer.is_value_supported] returns [code]false[/code] for every value and they are stored, but not pushed. The domain exists only when the engine is built with the [code]texture_streaming[/code] module, which needs a [RenderingDevice]: in the Web export, [code]Engine.has_singleton("TextureStreamingSettingsServer")[/code] returns [code]false[/code].
Values out of range are clamped with a warning: [code]memory_budget_mb[/code] [code]0[/code] to [code]65535[/code], [code]min_lod[/code] and [code]max_lod[/code] [code]0[/code] to [code]13[/code].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	if not Engine.has_singleton("TextureStreamingSettingsServer"):
		$Streaming.hide() # Built without the texture_streaming module (Web).
		return
	var streaming = Engine.get_singleton("TextureStreamingSettingsServer")
	$Streaming/Budget.value = streaming.get_memory_budget_mb()
	streaming.restart_required.connect(func(_names): $RestartHint.show())

func _on_budget_value_changed(value):
	Engine.get_singleton("TextureStreamingSettingsServer").set_memory_budget_mb(int(value))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    if (!Engine.HasSingleton("TextureStreamingSettingsServer"))
    {
        GetNode<Control>("Streaming").Hide(); // Built without the texture_streaming module (Web).
        return;
    }
    GodotObject streaming = Engine.GetSingleton("TextureStreamingSettingsServer");
    GetNode<SpinBox>("Streaming/Budget").Value = streaming.Call("get_memory_budget_mb").AsInt32();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Because the class is missing in some builds, code that must run in every build reaches it through [method Engine.get_singleton] and [method Object.call], as above. In builds with the module, C# also has the static class [code skip-lint]TextureStreamingSettingsServer[/code].
